This test is about Xe 390 keV  irradiation pure UO2 calculated with the SRIM like "Full Cascade" algorithm.

The input are given in Config.in. This file is internally decomposed into four temp_ifile.iradina which corresponds to the four files generated by the GUI. See this file for details about the input parameters

The main outputs are 
Xe3.9MeV.ions.total, implanted ion distribution
Xe3.9MeV.vac.sum, total vacancy concentration
Xe3.9MeV.vac.z8.m15.999.mat0.elem1, O (Z=8) vacancy concentration
Xe3.9MeV.vac.z92.m238.030.mat0.elem0, U (Z=92) vacancy concentration.
Additional files *repl* and *int* are for "replacements" and "interstitials". 

Each file has four columns, Columns 1 to 3 are interger index of the cells. In the present calculation only column 1 is relevant. To transform the integer index into nm multiply by 1 (one), into Angstrom multiply by 10. These factors depend on the size of the cells given in Confing.in/ temp_structfile.iradina
Column4 gives the concentrations of ions or vacancies. 
In Xe3.9MeV.ions.total, the concentration of ions is expressed in (ions/cm3) per (ions/cm2), i.e. in cm-1.
In Xe3.9MeV.vac.*, the concentration of vacancies is expressed in (vacancies/cm3) per (ions/cm2), i.e. in cm-1.

Figures (*.png) and corresponding xmgrace graphs are plots of the outputs files (x=column one ; y=column 4). In "raw" figures the files are directly plotted. in rescaled figures, x is rescaled to Angstron (*10), y is rescaled in Angstroms-1 (*1e-8).


